        "original_id": "b4f8c8ec-f558-5606-9c31-a3854769d1fd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Oliver Boot, Molière, Peter Abelard\n- Works: Antony and Cleopatra, In Extremis, Three Musketeers, Hayfever, Tartuffe, Jamaica Inn, Othello\n- Organizations: Cheek by Jowl\n- Topics: Theatre credits, theatrical comedy\n\nFacts:\n- Tartuffe, or The Impostor, or The Hypocrite, was first performed in 1664.\n- Molière wrote Tartuffe, which is one of his most famous theatrical comedies.\n- Oliver Boot’s theatre credits include Antony and Cleopatra, Three Musketeers, Hayfever, Tartuffe, and Jamaica Inn.\n- Oliver Boot appeared in In Extremis in the role of Abelard.\n- Oliver Boot performed in an award-winning world tour of Othello with Cheek by Jowl.",
